# Data is read as a whole before the code runs over it (the author 2026-11-11, LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#call-receivers;
# the book, call-receivers): a variable has no visibility "forward" or "backward" -- a name used above the line of its
# declaration reads the same place of the data. A literal value is data and stands in its place from the start (R12):
# Self reads x = 5 above `int: x 5`, and Code reads the x of the Data it was given. A computed declaration is code,
# executed at its line (computed_self_refused, computed_data_refused, computed_line_publishes).
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
sub: main () (
    Self:
        y := x + 1
        int: x 5
        int: y
    Code:
        y := x + 1
        int: x
        int: y
    Data:
        int: x 5
        int: y 0
)
    call: Self
    call: Data Code
main()
int: literal_above main\data\Self\y
int: supplied_above main\data\Data\y
int: self_x main\data\Self\x
int: data_x main\data\Data\x
